webiq.snippet:
The Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) has issued a final rule mandating certain airport certificate holders to develop, implement, maintain, and adhere to an airport safety management system (SMS). ... - submit an implementation plan for approval within 12-24 months;
- submit an Airport Certification Manual amendment/SMS manual 12 months after implementation plan approval; and
- fully implement the SMS within 36 months of the implementation plan's approval. ... Of the approximately 550 U.S. airports that fall under the FAA's federal airport certification regulation, 258 are required to follow the SMS rules.
